{"name":"Golden History","hex":"#bb993a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"history","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The aggregate of past events, both unrecorded and recorded.","The empirical study of past events, as distinct from literature, myth, or scripture; the assessment of notable events."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To narrate or record."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/history"}],"entries":[{"title":"History","blocks":[{"text":"History is the systematic study of the past, focusing primarily on the human past. As an academic discipline, it analyses and interprets evidence to construct narratives about what happened and explain why it happened. Some theorists categorize history as a social science, while others see it as part of the humanities or consider it a hybrid discipline. Similar debates surround the purpose of history—for example, whether its main aim is theoretical, to uncover the truth, or practical, to learn lessons from the past. In a more general sense, the term history refers not to an academic field but to the past itself, times in the past, or to individual texts about the past."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Carstian_Luyckx_-_Still_life_with_a_globe%2C_books%2C_shells_and_corals_resting_on_a_stone_ledge.jpg/330px-Carstian_Luyckx_-_Still_life_with_a_globe%2C_books%2C_shells_and_corals_resting_on_a_stone_ledge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History","wikidata":"Q309"},{"title":"Gol